; firms.vla - the firms' styles: the Firms sheet, the four answers to the Series 777's
; last question, ungraded, "Which best describes you?", each the style of the firm it
; founds (docs/OMAKASE.md, GUARD.1 and BACK.2). Words alone: one macro named after this
; file, whose body is one call of the library's strings. The source includes this file
; after its manifest, with every other include, and calls (firms) where the sheet's
; rows belong. The exam shows the first four rows as the question's options, a row's
; place its letter, and the certificate the one chosen; the firms' own names come with
; BACK.2, a field beside the style. To add a row, read README.md beside this file.

(defmacro (firms)
  "the firms' styles: the Firms sheet, a style a row, the exam's last question's options"
  (strings "Firms"                  ; the sheet, hidden among the tabs
    ("Style" 40)                    ; its field, its header and its width in characters: the style, as a candidate describes it
    ; each row: its one field, the style in the candidate's own words
    ("I read the prospectus")
    ("I read the headlines")
    ("I read the room")
    ("I feel the market")
    ))                              ; the sheet's end: a style added goes above this line
